      "id": "78f7630a472f6224a3682f1ab6561e65",
      "title": "US Stock Market: Berkshire steps up buybacks, boosts Alphabet stake as cash falls",
      "description": "Berkshire Hathaway began deploying its cash pile in Q2, buying nearly $20 billion more stocks than it sold and ending a 14-quarter selling streak. It also repurchased $4.5 billion of its own shares in Q2 and bought about $10 billion of Alphabet stock, while posting better-than-expected operating profit.",
      "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/us-stocks/news/us-stock-market-berkshire-steps-up-buybacks-boosts-alphabet-stake-as-cash-falls/articleshow/133086633.cms",
